Subject: [PATCH] speech: profile voices must come from a real provider

The profile's speech.voices list filters the voices that real providers
register, by name, language and optional local_service. It never adds a
voice, and voice IDs, metadata and order come from the provider. If no
registered voice matches, speak() fails through the normal error
callback and does not fall back to the default voice. An empty list
allows no voices, and an absent list keeps the host's voices.

